WEBVTT

15
00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.390
<v SPEAKER 1> I've been meaning to ask you for some advice about restaurants.

16
00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:48.190
<v SPEAKER 1> I need to book somewhere to celebrate my sister's 30th birthday and I liked the sound of that place you went to for your mum's 50th.

17
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.070
<v SPEAKER 2> The Junction?

18
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:52.550
<v SPEAKER 2> Yeah, I'd definitely recommend that for a special occasion.

19
00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.370
<v SPEAKER 2> We had a great time there.

20
00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.390
<v SPEAKER 2> Everyone really enjoyed it.

21
00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:57.930
<v SPEAKER 1> Where is it again?

22
00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:58.990
<v SPEAKER 1> I can't remember.

23
00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:04.250
<v SPEAKER 2> It's on Grayson Street, only about a two-minute walk from the station.

24
00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:05.690
<v SPEAKER 1> Oh, that's good.

25
00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.130
<v SPEAKER 1> I'd prefer not to have to drive anywhere.

26
00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:11.350
<v SPEAKER 1> But I don't want to have to walk too far either.

27
00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:17.470
<v SPEAKER 2> Yes, the location's perfect, but that's not necessarily why I'd recommend it.

28
00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.730
<v SPEAKER 2> The food's amazing.

29
00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:25.410
<v SPEAKER 2> If you like fish, it's probably the best restaurant in town for that.

30
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:30.970
<v SPEAKER 2> It's always really fresh and there are lots of interesting dishes to choose from.

31
00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.630
<v SPEAKER 2> But all the food is good there.

32
00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.530
<v SPEAKER 1> Is it really expensive?

33
00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.450
<v SPEAKER 2> It's certainly not cheap, but for a special occasion I think it's fine.

34
00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:48.570
<v SPEAKER 2> It's got a great atmosphere and before dinner you can go up on the roof and have a drink.

35
00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:52.570
<v SPEAKER 2> It's really nice up there, but you need to book.

36
00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.430
<v SPEAKER 2> It's very popular as the views are spectacular.

37
00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.110
<v SPEAKER 1> Sounds good.

38
00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.970
<v SPEAKER 1> So that's definitely a possibility then.

39
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.890
<v SPEAKER 1> Is there anywhere else you can think of?

40
00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:09.630
<v SPEAKER 2> Um, if you want somewhere a bit less formal, then you could try Paloma.

41
00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:10.970
<v SPEAKER 1> Where's that?

42
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.210
<v SPEAKER 1> I haven't heard of it.

43
00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.670
<v SPEAKER 2> No, it's quite new.

44
00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.390
<v SPEAKER 2> It's only been open a few months, but it's got a great reputation already.

45
00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:22.930
<v SPEAKER 2> It's in a really beautiful old building on Bow Street.

46
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.870
<v SPEAKER 1> Oh, I think I know where you mean.

47
00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.810
<v SPEAKER 1> Right beside the cinema.

48
00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.330
<v SPEAKER 2> Yes, that's it.

49
00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:33.590
<v SPEAKER 2> I've only been there a couple of times, but I was really impressed.

50
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:37.710
<v SPEAKER 2> The chef used to work at Don Felipe's apparently.

51
00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:40.710
<v SPEAKER 2> I was really sorry when that closed down.

52
00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.850
<v SPEAKER 1> So is all the food they serve Spanish then?

53
00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:50.870
<v SPEAKER 2> Yeah, you can get lots of small dishes to share, which always works really well if you're in a group.

54
00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.910
<v SPEAKER 1> Hmm, worth thinking about.

55
00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:57.750
<v SPEAKER 2> Yeah, there's a lively atmosphere and the waiters are really friendly.

56
00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:03.450
<v SPEAKER 2> The only thing is that you need to pay a £50 deposit to book a table.

57
00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.150
<v SPEAKER 1> A lot of restaurants are doing that these days.

58
00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:11.210
<v SPEAKER 1> I should have a look at the menu to check there's a good choice of vegetarian dishes.

59
00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.590
<v SPEAKER 1> A couple of my friends have stopped eating meat.

60
00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:16.070
<v SPEAKER 2> Not sure.

61
00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:18.970
<v SPEAKER 2> I'd say the selection of those would be quite limited.

62
00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:29.210
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 5 to 10.

63
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:03.310
Now listen and answer questions 5 to 10.

64
00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:08.550
<v SPEAKER 2> I've just thought of another idea.

65
00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.690
<v SPEAKER 2> Have you been to the Audley?

66
00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.410
<v SPEAKER 1> No, don't think I've heard of it.

67
00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.070
<v SPEAKER 1> How's it spelt?

68
00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:19.930
<v SPEAKER 2> A-U-D-L-E-Y.

69
00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.890
<v SPEAKER 2> You must have heard of it.

70
00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.250
<v SPEAKER 2> There's been a lot about it in the press.

71
00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.650
<v SPEAKER 1> I don't tend to pay much attention to that kind of thing.

72
00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.130
<v SPEAKER 1> So where is it exactly?

73
00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.270
<v SPEAKER 2> It's in that hotel near Baxter Bridge, on the top floor.

74
00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:38.650
<v SPEAKER 1> Oh, the views would be incredible from up there.

75
00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:40.590
<v SPEAKER 2> Yeah, I'd love to go.

76
00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:47.310
<v SPEAKER 2> I can't think of the chef's name, but she was a judge on that TV cookery show recently.

77
00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.310
<v SPEAKER 2> And she's written a couple of cookery books.

78
00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.790
<v SPEAKER 1> Oh, Angela Frayne.

79
00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:53.810
<v SPEAKER 2> That's the one.

80
00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:58.730
<v SPEAKER 2> Anyway, it's had excellent reviews from all the newspapers.

81
00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.250
<v SPEAKER 1> That would be a memorable place for a celebration.

82
00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.290
<v SPEAKER 2> Definitely.

83
00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:10.450
<v SPEAKER 2> Obviously it's worth going there just for the view, but the food is supposed to be really special.

84
00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:14.770
<v SPEAKER 1> She only likes cooking with local products, doesn't she?

85
00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:15.470
<v SPEAKER 2> Yes.

86
00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:23.830
<v SPEAKER 2> Everything at the restaurant has to be sourced within a short distance, and absolutely nothing flown in from abroad.

87
00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.630
<v SPEAKER 1> I imagine it's really expensive though.

88
00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.870
<v SPEAKER 2> Well, you could go for the set lunch.

89
00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.370
<v SPEAKER 2> That's quite reasonable for a top-class restaurant.

90
00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.210
<v SPEAKER 2> Thirty pounds a head.

91
00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:39.630
<v SPEAKER 2> In the evening, I think it'd be more like fifty pounds.

92
00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.970
<v SPEAKER 1> At least that, I should think.

93
00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.810
<v SPEAKER 1> But I'm sure everyone would enjoy it.

94
00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.150
<v SPEAKER 1> It's not the kind of place you leave feeling hungry though, is it?

95
00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.650
<v SPEAKER 1> With tiny portions.

96
00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:54.050
<v SPEAKER 2> No, the reviews I've read didn't mention that.

97
00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:56.890
<v SPEAKER 2> I imagine they'd be average.

98
00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.210
<v SPEAKER 1> Well, that's all great.

99
00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:00.710
<v SPEAKER 1> Thanks so much.
